      "estimated_duration_s": 24,
      "narration_text": "What to retry is a decision, not a default. Timeouts, rate limits and server errors get retried, with a wait that doubles each time, plus a little randomness, so clients that failed together don't all come back together. But a four hundred means my request is wrong. Retrying just wastes arXiv's time, so it fails at once, with arXiv's own message.",
