      "estimated_duration_s": 26,
      "narration_text": "Then the save itself. Instead of checking each paper and then inserting it, one statement upserts the whole day: insert, and on conflict, update. It's atomic, so a failed run saves nothing and can simply run again. And it's safe to repeat. I ran September first twice: still two hundred forty-three rows, all refreshed, no duplicates.",
